{:adr-id "2625000000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-9820 (undifferentiated service-producing activities of private households for own use) household time-use-survey-programme coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-16"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607121000" "ADR-2607152500"]
 :template-repo "cloud-itonami-isic-873 (module structure mirrored module-for-module)"

 :context
 "ISIC 9820 is a UN SNA statistical bookkeeping category for own-account,
  non-market household service production (unpaid domestic/care work), not
  a real business -- there is no market entity a 9820 registration would
  correspond to. Registry :name was truncated (10% seed-data bug),
  corrected here. A separate redundant :id \"982\" group entry exists and
  is intentionally left untouched. Rather than fabricate a marketplace
  business, this actor is scoped honestly as operations-coordination for a
  national-statistics-office style time-use survey/tracking programme (UN/
  OECD time-use survey methodology), paralleling the sibling ISIC 9810
  (own-account goods production) actor's framing without depending on its
  code. Part of cloud-itonami Wave 4 (person-facing) under ADR-2607152500's
  P3/P4-parallel amendment, which mandates: closed op-allowlist never
  includes an op that directly finalizes a welfare-intervention decision;
  any concern-flagging op always escalates, never auto-commit-eligible."

 :self-tripping-bug-research
 "During this build, proactively checked this actor family's known
  self-tripping bug class (bare-noun scope-exclusion terms matching the
  advisor's own default disclaimer text) against the cloud-itonami-isic-873
  reference/template repo itself. Found a live, previously undetected
  instance: 873's governor scope-excluded-terms includes bare \"薬\"
  (medicine/drug), which matches inside its own :coordinate-supply-request
  advisor rationale (\"...非医薬品消耗品の調達調整のみ。投薬なし。\"),
  reproduced via REPL script against a fresh clone of that repo
  (gov/check on adv/infer's own output -> :hard? true, :scope-excluded,
  for :coordinate-supply-request; :hard? false for the other four ops).
  873's own test suite passes because no test pipes advisor/infer's literal
  output through governor/check for that op. Not fixed here (out of scope
  for this actor/ADR) -- recorded as the concrete evidence motivating this
  actor's own term-phrasing discipline below."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["finalizing any welfare-intervention decision (child protective action, elder/adult protective action, custody removal, protective-order issuance) -- always HARD, permanent block, independent of op or confidence"
  "clinical/medical decisions"
  "any direct actuation outside :effect :propose"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-9820 (timeuseops.* namespace) mirroring
  cloud-itonami-isic-873's module shape module-for-module: Store, Advisor,
  Governor, Phase, Operation (fully-wired langgraph-clj StateGraph with
  real interrupt-before/resume, not a stub), Sim.
  - Store: households keyed by string :household-id, :registered?/
    :verified? programme-enrollment flags, append-only ledger +
    coordination-log.
  - Advisor: 4 proposal ops (log-time-use-record, schedule-survey-visit,
    coordinate-programme-support, flag-welfare-concern), all :effect
    :propose, all disclaiming finalization authority in rationale text
    without ever using the governor's scanned finalization-ACTION phrases.
  - Governor (TimeUseProgrammeGovernor): 4 HARD checks (household-
    unverified, effect-not-propose, op-not-allowed,
    welfare-intervention-finalization-blocked) + 3 escalation gates
    (flag-welfare-concern always-escalate, coordinate-programme-support
    cost > 300 threshold, confidence < 0.6 floor).
    welfare-intervention-finalization-terms are phrased as
    finalization/execution ACTIONS ('finalize welfare intervention',
    'authorize custody removal', 'issue a protective order'), never bare
    nouns -- the specific discipline that avoids the self-tripping bug
    documented above. Dedicated regression test
    (governor-test/default-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion)
    runs the default advisor's own proposal for every allowed op (incl.
    flag-welfare-concern, whose legitimate rationale discusses welfare
    concerns) through the governor and asserts none is ever HARD-blocked
    by op-not-allowed or welfare-intervention-finalization-blocked.
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate; flag-welfare-concern permanently absent from
    every phase's :auto set (governor + phase both independently enforce).
  - Operation: advisor -> governor -> phase-gate -> commit|hold|escalate,
    interrupt-before #{:request-approval} for real human-in-the-loop.
  - Sim: demo runner covering clean auto-commits, over-threshold
    escalation, always-escalate welfare-concern flag, and all 4 HARD-hold
    scenarios.
  - Tests: 45 tests / 137 assertions, all green (advisor, governor incl.
    self-trip regression + positive-detection tests, phase,
    governor-contract full-graph integration, store-contract).
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later.
  - README Scope section states the residual/statistical framing
    explicitly and honestly. GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY/
    CODE_OF_CONDUCT written fresh for this actor's actual scope (873's own
    copies were found to still describe an unrelated ISIC 0520
    lignite-mining actor, a copy-paste bug deliberately not repeated)."

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["ISIC 9820 now has an honest, precedented real-world framing (time-use survey programme) instead of a fabricated marketplace, stated explicitly in the README"
   "Mandatory Wave 4 person-facing guardrail (no welfare-intervention finalization in the op allowlist, flag-welfare-concern always escalates) hardcoded in a dedicated, independently-testable governor rule with terms phrased to avoid this fleet's known self-tripping bug class, verified by a dedicated regression test plus positive-detection tests"
   "flag-welfare-concern structurally excluded from every phase's auto-commit set by two independent layers (governor always-escalate-ops + phase auto sets)"
   "Portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings"
   "Proactively found and documented (though did not fix, out of scope) a live instance of the self-tripping bug in the very reference/template repo this build mirrors"]
  :negative
  ["Real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up (in-memory MemStore for now)"
   "cloud-itonami-isic-873's own bare-noun self-tripping bug (\"薬\" matching its own :coordinate-supply-request rationale) is documented but not fixed by this ADR -- a future pass on that specific repo has a concrete repro"]}

